{
  "assessment": "This change adds `crm/keys.py`, introducing a folding utility and a merge key function intended to canonicalize email-based identity resolution. However, `merge_key` returns the raw email string instead of calling `fold_email`, so the canonicalization logic is effectively disabled at the point of merging. Because no other files were updated in this diff to consume `fold_email` or replace their current raw-key lookups, downstream duplicate customers will continue to be created on casing/whitespace differences.",
  "findings": [
    {
      "actual": "' A@b.com '",
      "at": "crm/keys.py::merge_key",
      "call": "python -c \"from crm.keys import merge_key; print(repr(merge_key({'email': ' A@b.com '})))\"",
      "defect": "`merge_key` fails to apply email folding, defeating the purpose of the new module and leaving the duplicate customer bug unaddressed when this key is used for merging.",
      "expected": "'a@b.com'"
    }
  ]
}
